 class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operator<span class=\"sy2\">/</span></span></code>, e.g., <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/month\"><span class=\"kw2625\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">April</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">/</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2583\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">Sunday</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/operator_slash\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator/</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  conventional syntax for Gregorian calendar date creation <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/month_weekday","title":"std::chrono::month_weekday"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::month_weekday::month_weekday","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Constructs a month_weekday object that stores the month m and the weekday_indexed wdi."},{"label":"Notes","note":"A more convenient way to construct a month_weekday is with operator/, e.g., std::chrono::April/std::chrono::Sunday[2]."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator/","note":"conventional syntax for Gregorian calendar date creation"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":50,"codeBlockCount":0}
